  "notes": [
    "The master key is a specification test key, not a real one: its bytes spell out what it is. Every epoch key, slot and padding leaf here follows from it, so the whole tree is reproducible. A real k_master never appears in this repository (INV-TREE-05).",
    "The full leaf set is recorded where capacity allows it, so a disagreement localises to a slot rather than to the root. Above 256 slots only the root, the assignment and the proofs are kept.",
    "Every leaf is padding derived from the epoch key, so the account this epoch publishes and the instruction that publishes it are the same length and the same layout as a full epoch's, and differ only inside `root`. That is the indistinguishable footprint §4.3 asks for and what V-Z-01's count-hiding rests on.",
    "There are no proofs because there is nothing to prove the inclusion of. An empty `proofs` array is this vector's content, not an omission from it."
  ],
